# The Distortion World (the original's PL_D_GIRATINA role): the reverse world behind Turnback Cave, where islands of
# rock float upside down, waterfalls run sideways and Giratina keeps its own laws of time and space. One whole-tone
# melody heard three ways, as the world turns it: first as it is, a hollow ocarina over a low D pedal while harp runs
# float upwards; then upside down, the horn singing its inversion while the pedal moves to the top of the strings,
# the bass falls away and the runs fall instead; then backwards and a semitone higher in the other whole-tone scale,
# brass, choir and timpani over an E-flat pedal, with a clock that ticks in threes against the four. A whole-tone
# scale has no semitones, so nothing in a section rubs, and nothing ever resolves; a shaker swells as if played in
# reverse into each turn, and the E-flat sinks back to D to begin again. Original composition for this game.
title Distortion World
tempo 76
meter 4/4
reverb 0.55
night none

